        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0543" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.841 Surtax/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-09T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1927—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 9—5:58 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>711. Legation’s 705, July 8, 3 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I earnestly request authorization to inform the consul general at Shanghai
                        that his recommendation is approved with regard to informing the Customs
                        that American ships will pay tonnage dues at treaty rates and that if
                        payment is refused they will proceed without Customs clearance
                        papers.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Surtax on tonnage dues will be discussed at a meeting of the diplomatic
                        body on July 11th and as there is hardly time to receive your instructions
                        by that date the Legation will reserve the position of the American
                        Government.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
